WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
What the fuck is this?

00:07.000 --> 00:12.000
This is Kailos.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.000
His new model looks so good, man.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
I did not expect to see you again so soon, my friend.

00:20.000 --> 00:24.000
After you'd answered the call of the irons.

00:24.000 --> 00:27.000
Something has happened, Katkar.

00:27.000 --> 00:30.000
Something terrible.

00:30.000 --> 00:34.000
Kalakos, tell me.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.000
It all happened so quickly.

00:37.000 --> 00:48.000
And Rathien, young as he is, bravely or perhaps foolishly tried to stop it.

00:48.000 --> 00:49.000
But he was too late.

00:49.000 --> 00:52.000
Did you hit him in the head with a rock?

00:52.000 --> 00:53.000
The tempest.

00:53.000 --> 01:05.000
Oh shit.

01:05.000 --> 01:09.000
We should have killed him.

01:09.000 --> 01:11.000
Oh, here we go.

01:11.000 --> 01:20.000
Oh.

01:20.000 --> 01:26.000
It's a rock guy from the cinematic Stonebrow.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.000
Who is she?

01:27.000 --> 01:29.000
What is she?

01:29.000 --> 01:36.000
She is Razageth, youngest of the primal Incarnates.

01:36.000 --> 01:38.000
Incarnates?

01:38.000 --> 01:43.000
Four dangerous adherents of the elemental forces.

01:43.000 --> 01:49.000
At the dawn of the aspects, our flights embraced the titans gifts.

01:49.000 --> 01:52.000
They did not.

01:52.000 --> 01:57.000
The war that followed was unimaginable.

01:57.000 --> 02:01.000
And it took all of our strength combined to banish them.

02:01.000 --> 02:08.000
If they were so dangerous, why were they not destroyed?

02:08.000 --> 02:11.000
I hadn't the heart to do it.

02:11.000 --> 02:15.000
We were once as clutchmates.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.000
So it's her sister.

02:16.000 --> 02:20.000
Time, it seems, has not quelled their fury.

02:20.000 --> 02:22.000
And look at us.

02:22.000 --> 02:27.000
Should she free her kin now, we haven't the strength to stop them.

02:27.000 --> 02:31.000
And if Iridicrum's hunger is unleashed.

02:31.000 --> 02:34.000
Then we have no choice.

02:34.000 --> 02:43.000
If we are to be protect us once more, the aspects of our dragon flights must be made anew.

02:43.000 --> 02:46.000
So they're going to undo that cataclysm shit?

02:46.000 --> 02:49.000
Our queen is determined, Kedgar.

02:49.000 --> 02:53.000
But we've only just begun to find who we are again.

02:53.000 --> 03:03.000
And I fear that without help, we may never get the chance to see our future secured.

03:03.000 --> 03:05.000
Hmm.				

03:05.000 --> 03:10.000
This is staff.

03:10.000 --> 03:25.000
Then it seems the mortal races too must answer the call and face the storms ahead.

03:25.000 --> 03:35.000
That's a good, that's a good one. Yeah.

